.env*
# ...but `.env-*-example` files are COMMITTED TEMPLATES, not secrets: every key
# present with a __FILL_...__ placeholder value, per documentation/secrets.md.
# devops/secrets.sh refuses to apply a file that still contains a placeholder,
# which is what makes an unsupplied value a loud failure instead of a silent one.
!.env-*-example
# alertmanager directory is now version-controlled
# Only ignore the secret.yaml file (tracked in root .gitignore)
